symbols.doc:
Register trusted domain code, not model-submitted functions or authority.

validate(i,r,unit) checks the owner's actual candidate contract;
basis(i,r,unit) returns only premises whose changes invalidate interpretation;
apply(i,r,unit,approval) returns the two roots using that same owner contract.
ENGINE supplies configuration's existing configure consumer through this API.

Call the narrow PowerShell scheduler adapter and decode its JSON result.

Only ``install`` uses the configured interval and operator timeout;
configuration validation already checked their ranges.

The first supervision blocker present in ``facts``, or None.

Facts without ``held`` or ``operator_enabled`` never report those blockers;
a persisted-state view or an explicit engine start omits them.

Completion evidence names a supplied record or a returned result, not a path or event.

The producer passes its input's supplied_record_ids with the task's result IDs;
the receiver passes current record IDs with the same result IDs.

Author one interpretation of the input ``UC-input`` on a ``routing_engine``; returns ``(bundle, check action)``.

With ``clarification`` the interpretation asks one blocking question ``Q-one``;
``payload`` is the proposed change of its single unit ``IU-one``.

``(engine, bundle, request)``: a bare engine holding ``record_fixtures.checked_import``'s state.

``request`` is the user's later exact approval in the public decision shape;
completing the initial intent and activation are recorded, not performed.

``tracker.observe`` of ``event`` as the next one-byte stream row, received at the tracker's clock.

A runner delivers every row with its stream coordinate (``ObservationBatch.source``);
this gives a unit test that same coordinate without a stream file.

files.doc:
Integration bundles: how a producer response is split into bundles, checked, previewed and applied.

Bundles are applied through the installed ``integration`` module over in-memory or real Git state;
receipts, retries and partial acceptance are asserted on the state each application leaves.

Host-capacity scheduling with real reservation arithmetic.

Lifecycle and input-currentness predicates are explicit preconditions here;
this test does not claim to validate authority or process termination.
